Subject: [PATCH] runtime: recognize Linux ARM64 cross-component hosts

Backport the aarch64 host detection already present in the pinned .NET 9 VMR.
This retains the existing cross-component tool graph for a native ARM64 build
that uses a target sysroot. It does not change the target ABI configuration.

Upstream-Reference: https://github.com/dotnet/dotnet/blob/v9.0.123/src/runtime/eng/native/configureplatform.cmake#L30
Base-VMR: 7d1bf90885cff22e7da72b27e9848e42fd3cb1ae

diff --git a/src/runtime/eng/native/configureplatform.cmake b/src/runtime/eng/native/configureplatform.cmake
--- a/src/runtime/eng/native/configureplatform.cmake
+++ b/src/runtime/eng/native/configureplatform.cmake
@@ -27,6 +27,8 @@ if(CLR_CMAKE_HOST_OS STREQUAL linux)
             endif()
         elseif(CMAKE_HOST_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR STREQUAL i686)
             set(CLR_CMAKE_HOST_UNIX_X86 1)
+        elseif(CMAKE_HOST_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR STREQUAL aarch64)
+            set(CLR_CMAKE_HOST_UNIX_ARM64 1)
         else()
             clr_unknown_arch()
         endif()
